Atlas overlay patch 0001: privacy/dnt-default-on
Why: every profile, new and existing, sends Do Not Track unless the person turns it off. A
first-run preference only reaches new profiles and stores an explicit value, so the default itself
changes (patches-0 P-01). The pref keeps its SYNCABLE_PREF flag.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
Test filter: *DoNotTrack*; journey J-A2 (request header DNT: 1)
Rebase risk: L (one line; the inherited GPC pref patch adds the line below it)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunk in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@
   registry->RegisterDictionaryPref(prefs::kBrowserWindowPlacementPopup);
   registry->RegisterDictionaryPref(prefs::kAppWindowPlacement);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kEnableDoNotTrack, false,
+      prefs::kEnableDoNotTrack, true,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumGlobalPrivacyControl, false);
 #if !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
